--- !u!102 &6082973476341002626
TextMesh:
  serializedVersion: 3
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1677108848622428769}
  m_Text: "Thank you for downloading the assets!\nFor intended visuals in Built-in
    Renderer, I recommend importing and setting up Unity's Post-Processing \npackage.
    \n\nDetailed instructions and recommended settings for your project\nto achieve
    better visuals similar to screenshots:\n\n1. Import the Post Processing package
    from Package Manager\n2. Select the Main Camera, click on the Layer dropout menu
    and select Add Layer then\ncreate a layer named PostProcessing.\n3. Select back
    the Main Camera and change its layer to the one you created\n4. Add Post-Process
    Layer component to the camera and set the Layer setting to the\nlayer you created\n5.
    Create new empty game object, rename it to PostProcessing Volume, set it's layer\nto
    PostProcessing\n6. Add Post-process Volume component and enable Is Global checkbox.\n7.
    Set the profile to fwOF_PostProcessing_01.\n\nNote: to control the wind use the
    TriForge Wind Controller script. You will also need\nto add it into any new scene
    you create with these assets if you wish to configure the wind.\n\nIf you have
    any questions or need support with the assets you can reach out to\nsupport@triforge.eu\nFor
    support requests remember to include your Unity version, the render pipeline
    and its\nversion as well as purchase invoice number to speed up the process."
  m_OffsetZ: 0
  m_CharacterSize: 1
  m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Anchor: 0
  m_Alignment: 0
  m_TabSize: 4
  m_FontSize: 50
  m_FontStyle: 0
  m_RichText: 1
  m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
  m_Color:
    serializedVersion: 2
    rgba: 4294967295
